{%- comment -%}
  Hands the shipping contract to JavaScript.

  The cart drawer is built client-side from /cart.js, which does not return product tags —
  it returns the hidden `_ship` line property the product form set. So the drawer needs the
  group→wording map too, and it used to carry its own copy of the rates in theme.js. That
  was a third place a rate could be changed in, and the only one a Liquid grep would miss.

  Rendered once in the layout as `window.ABM_SHIP`. theme.js falls back to its own defaults
  if this is ever absent, so the drawer degrades rather than breaking.

  Group ids match snippets/shipping-class.liquid. Rates match content/freight.json, which
  scripts/check_contracts.py enforces.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  window.ABM_SHIP = {
    "freight": { "rates": { "freight299": "$299.99", "freight199": "$199.99" } },
    "labels": {
      "pickup": "Pickup only",
      "freight299": "$299.99 freight",
      "freight199": "$199.99 freight",
      "free": "Free shipping"
    }
  };
</script>
